{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Vanessa in Cooking School: Indian Food"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Catching Up"}, {"type": "position", "content": 11}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 7}, {"type": "level", "content": "A2.1"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Accurately use information about travel and vacations in social situations."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations."}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Much, Many, Some, Any"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "Much and many are quantifiers. You use <span class=\"italic\">many</span> with count nouns to talk about the number of items.  You use <span class=\"italic\">much</span> with non-count nouns to talk about the amount or quantity of an item.<br>   <br>You can also use <span class=\"italic\">some</span> and <span class=\"italic\">any.</span> The words <span class=\"italic\">some</span> and <span class=\"italic\">any</span> are used for count and non-count nouns.  <span class=\"italic\">Some</span> means <span class=\"strong\">a few</span> or <span class=\"strong\">a little</span>. <span class=\"italic\">Any</span> can mean <span class=\"strong\">none</span> or <span class=\"strong\">a few</span> or <span class=\"strong\">a little</span>.<br>  <br>When you use <span class=\"italic\">any</span> in a question, it means a few. In a negative sentence, it means none.<br> "}, {"type": "example", "content": "There are many dishes from India."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Did you buy any vegetables?"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Some dishes don't have much meat in them."}, {"type": "example", "content": "There was so much meat!"}, {"type": "example", "content": "There isn't any here."}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Talking About Future Plans"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use the Present Continuous tense to talk about:<br>  <br><ul><li>events happening now, or</li> <li>planned events in the near future</li></ul></br>  When you talk about events in the near future, you use time markers and prepositions of time like: <br>  <br> <ul><li>in _____ minutes/hours/days</li> <li>this morning/afternoon/evening</li> <li>tonight</li> <li>tomorrow</li> <li>on Tuesday (a future day or date)</li></ul></br>"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "Indian"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "relating to India "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I love Indian food."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le07ob11aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use to talk about food, customs and traditions."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "heritage"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the traditional customs of a country"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: It was about Indian heritage. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le07ob11aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "bazaar"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "an area where there are a lot of small shops"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: There is a bazaar where you can buy many things."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le07ob11aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "jewelry"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "small things that you wear for decoration"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: All this jewelry was made in India."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le07ob11aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "shawl"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a piece of cloth that you can wear around the shoulders or head"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I bought a beautiful silk shawl. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le07ob11aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "takeout"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "food you buy at a restaurant to eat at home"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I want to buy takeout."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le07ob11aud06"}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn4le07ob11re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Choose a popular city in the world."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Go on the internet and research this city."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Answer these questions: <ul><li>What kinds of food are popular in this city?</li> <li>What traditions and customs are popular in this city?</li>  <li>Are there any famous places there?</li></ul>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write 5-6 sentences. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Read them aloud to your class. "}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I read about a city."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I answer questions about food, customs and traditions."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I write sentences about foods, places, customs and traditions."}]}], "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"_data": [], "id": 0, "type": "welcome", "contents": [{}], "template_override": 1}, {"id": 1, "type": "audio", "title": "", "_data": [], "template_override": 1, "contents": [{"type": "slideshow", "value": {"audiosrc": "engenn4le07ob11re2aud01", "coverimg": "engenn4le07ob11re2img05.jpg", "images": [{"text": "", "id": 0, "time": "0", "image": "engenn4le07ob11re2img05.jpg"}, {"text": "<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: Hey! How's cooking school?<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Cooking school is okay but so much homework!<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: You're getting lots of practice though.", "id": 1, "time": "100", "image": "engenn4le07ob11re2img05.jpg"}, {"text": "<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: What are you doing? <br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: I'm sitting in a train and eating curry. I love Indian food! <br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: San Francisco has a great Indian community and many festivals. In fact, I went to one by City Hall this weekend. <br>", "id": 2, "time": "9000", "image": "engenn4le07ob11re2img05.jpg"}, {"text": "<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: What's that?<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: It was about Indian heritage. There were so many things!", "id": 3, "time": "24000", "image": "engenn4le07ob11re2img01.jpg"}, {"text": "<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: Did you buy any jewelry? <br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Yes! I walked around the bazaar. I bought many spices and some shawls. I ate so much food and there was so much meat! I'm attending a class about how to make a pie next week. I should make a meat one!<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: I'm getting some takeout when I arrive in London! We're arriving in London this evening.", "id": 4, "time": "30000", "image": "engenn4le07ob11re2img02.jpg"}]}}]}], "exercises": [{"questions": [], "stimuli_ids": [0], "id": 0, "type": "WLC", "img_path": "", "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can talk about food, places in a town, customs, and traditions."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can express general quantities."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can talk about what people are doing."}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "Where do you like to go with your friends around town?"}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "How often do you go out with your friends?"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Welcome"}]}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"allowed_attempts": 2, "correct_feedback": "Correct", "attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "You have 2 tries"}, {"type": "text", "content": "you have 1 attempt left"}], "incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "try again"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time"}]}}, {"type": "free_header_text", "content": "Ask your partner:"}, {"type": "free_type_text_area", "content": "Let's review!"}], "template_override": 1}, {"questions": [{"_data": [{"type": "question", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}]}], "id": 0, "responses": [{"correct": 0, "_data": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}], "id": 0, "selected": 0}, {"correct": 1, "_data": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}], "id": 1, "selected": 0}]}], "stimuli_ids": [1], "id": 1, "type": "STI", "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Sally and Vanessa <span class=\"tool-tip\" id=\"tip_1_0\">video chat</span> about their travels! "}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"type": "group_